# Console shutdown regression — the quit path (CTRL-Q / `:quit`).
#
#   bin/metatron-docker build console --steps bin/test/console-quit.steps
#
# Bug this guards: on quit, the process used to hand the tty back to the shell
# (and then exit) while the shutdown's own log line was still queued on the
# render thread (a daemon) — so `metatron successfully shutdown` landed either
# after the shell's prompt or not at all.  close() now drains the render queue
# before it gives the terminal back, so the line is on the wire before exit.
#
# The harness pumps the pty until the line appears OR the process dies, then
# re-checks once — so a line lost to the dying daemon thread fails the check
# deterministically, and a delivered one passes.

WAIT_CONSOLE

# --- the console is live before we ask it to go ---
MARK live
SEND 1
WAIT ==>1

# --- :quit: the shutdown log must be on the terminal before the process ends ---
MARK quit
SEND :quit
WAIT metatron successfully shutdown 40
